# HR-23 option (i): the pins of the project's Zeek build (brief P4-4-HR23,
# stage 3; docs/phase4/D4-hr23-design.md, section 4.5; D7's C1 to C6 in
# docs/phase4/D4-hr25-design.md, section 4). Read by build.sh, which stops
# at the first input that does not match.
#
# The release tarball and its signature, from the Zeek project's GitHub
# release v9.0.1. The tarball's SHA-256 is the one the design note and
# docs/phase4/D4-engine-linux-eval.md section 3 record.
ZEEK_TARBALL_URL=https://github.com/zeek/zeek/releases/download/v9.0.1/zeek-9.0.1.tar.gz
ZEEK_TARBALL_SHA256=fbee2eb5ee6ebd64ef0db830fbb9fa1d702d58807643c719e8338a59329197f2
ZEEK_ASC_URL=https://github.com/zeek/zeek/releases/download/v9.0.1/zeek-9.0.1.tar.gz.asc
ZEEK_ASC_SHA256=269e266a0b473b4621448034b98a9f8aafe39f0e53f026ad03bff5312e5bffce
# Zeek's public key, committed beside this file (zeek-release-key.asc), as
# keys.openpgp.org served it for the primary fingerprint below; D7 checked
# the signature with it (comment 6864785127 on #675). Its binding to the
# Zeek project rests on that one channel until a second source agrees (R-3
# in the design note). The build checks .asc with gpgv against this file
# only, never a default keyring and never a keyserver.
ZEEK_KEY_SHA256=10d83739443e4ded7e7ace657d807783043ae195cb00b4171e8a200aab4fa9a6
ZEEK_KEY_FPR=962FD2187ED5A1DD82FC478A33F15EAEF8CB8019
ZEEK_SIGNING_SUBKEY_FPR=E9690B2B7D8AC1A19F921C4AC68B494DF56ACC7E
# Zeek 9.0.1's COPYING, copied verbatim (D7's C5).
COPYING_SHA256=1f984adb6b5cd93d5035c2a87c2df5f38922649fbea90c7bd79ff321d17333aa
# Option (i)'s patch, with (B')'s catch in DNP3.cc, the project's own file.
HR23_PATCH_SHA256=493ddbdc3c0024c429593fca393f67ceb6acb3b724ac21f3371c39f2e7ec9410
# HR-25's option A with option (a), parts HR25-B1 and HR25-B2 (D4-124):
# applied after option (i)'s patch, in that fixed order, with no fuzz (the
# design's section 4, C1). C2A is the tree with both.
HR25_PATCH_SHA256=bf8fc9e8a4a5dfcce88cde8bb9cc70d03eb79c00c731e6a8840213811c359455
# A's mutant controls (controls/hr25-<name>.patch), each C2A with one
# control patch; never shipped. hr25_unit.py names the rule each breaks.
HR25_CONTROLS="no-mod64 append-at-tseq append-at-tseq2 no-seq-check append-repeat count-every-repeat cmp-number cmp-app-only cmp-transport cmp-shorter any-repeat ignore-fcb reset-keeps-fcb no-window window-once drop-keeps-window seg-lt-250 seg-249 fir-checked shared-tseq linkonly-clears link-length-lt6 scan-clears header-skip-10 header-skip-2 linkonly-ends-delivery chunk-crc-ends-delivery limit-ge limit-plus-one confirm-at-header weirds-before-confirm violation-before-confirm rows-before-confirm skip-before-confirm confirm-at-fir confirm-before-eof end-any-count end-five budget-f-7 budget-f-gt budget-no-violation budget-weird-gated budget-no-count budget-no-row budget-orig-only budget-o-2047 budget-o-gt scan-first-octet-free budget-o-not-in-scan embedded-free budget-at-delivery-end budget-no-skip fcm-each-charged fcm-octets-charged fcm-run-unbroken tseq-charges-fragment tseq-charges-two retry-charged confirm-reads-link-function direction-weird-ungated no-first-at-confirm interval-strict interval-twice interval-any-delivery interval-no-change-check mark-drop-only no-first-after-confirm scan-weird-each-octet"
# The base image of both build stages, by digest: debian:13-slim's
# linux/amd64 manifest on 2026-11-15, from Docker Hub's registry (the base
# Zeek's own docker/builder.Dockerfile and final.Dockerfile name). A
# first-use pin. The packages installed on it are not pinned by version:
# build.sh records each stage's dpkg list in the build record.
BASE_IMAGE=debian@sha256:7378260c0a098d27ac206225db5e7d92b8c7c84ea7afccc86eeb513756bbd392
